 years since China put tariffs on American-grown soybeans during a tit-for-tat trade war with then-President Donald Trump – and they remain in place despite the change in administrations.", "reference": "2022 May 8, Katie Lobosco, “Trump’s trade war looms over soybean farmers 4 years later”, in CNN, archived from the original on 22 Nov 2024:"}, {"text": "Four years ago, 57 million tuned in to the only vice presidential debate of the 2020 election cycle between Harris and then-Vice President Mike Pence.", "reference": "2024 October 2, Brian Stelter, “43 million watched Walz-Vance VP debate, in significant drop from 2020 matchup”, in CNN Business, archived from the original on 18 Feb 2025:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "тогавашен"}, {"language": {"code": "da", "name": "Danish"}, "word": "daværende"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "toenmalig"}, {"language": {"code": "eo", "name": "Esperanto"}, "word": "tiama"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "silloinen"}, {"language": {"code": "fr", "name": "French"}, "word": "d'alors"}, {"language": {"code": "ka", "name": "Georgian"}, "word": "მაშინდელი"}, {"language": {"code": "de", "name": "German"}, "word": "damalig"}, {"language": {"code": "el", "name": "Greek"}, "word": "αλλοτινός"}, {"language": {"code": "he", "name": "Hebrew"}, "word": "דְּאָז"}, {"language": {"code": "hu", "name": "Hungarian"}, "word": "akkori"}, {"language": {"code": "ja", "name": "Japanese"}, "word": "当時"}, {"language": {"code": "ja", "name": "Japanese"}, "word": "そのとき"}, {"language": {"code": "ja", "name": "Japanese"}, "word": "その時点"}, {"language": {"code": "nb", "name": "Norwegian Bokmål"}, "word": "daværende"}, {"language": {"code": "nn", "name": "Norwegian Nynorsk"}, "word": "dåværande"}, {"language": {"code": "pl", "name": "Polish"}, "word": "bieżący"}, {"language": {"code": "pt", "name": "Portuguese"}, "word": "então"}, {"language": {"code": "ro", "name": "Romanian"}, "word": "but see de atunci"}, {"language": {"code": "ru", "name": "Russian"}, "word": "тогда́шний"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "de entonces"}, {"language": {"code": "sv", "name": "Swedish"}, "word": "dåvarande"}, {"language": {"code": "tr", "name": "Turkish"}, "word": "o zamanki"}, {"language": {"code": "zza", "name": "Zazaki"}, "word": "wıni bı"}], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "noun", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ðɛn/", "tags": ["UK", "US"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ðen/", "tags": ["General Australian"]}], "forms": [{"word": "den", "tags": ["alternative"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "That time.", "tags": [], "examples": ["It will be finished before then."], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "това време"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "die tijd"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "se"}, {"language": {"code": "pt", "name": "Portuguese"}, "word": "então"}, {"language": {"code": "ro", "name": "Romanian"}, "word": "atunci"}, {"language": {"code": "es", "name": "Spanish"}, "word": "entonces"}, {"language": {"code": "zza", "name": "Zazaki"}, "word": "a çerğ"}], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}, {"language": {"code": "en", "name": "English"}, "partOfSpeech": "conjunction", "pronunciations": [{"type": "ipa", "text": "/ðɛn/", "tags": ["UK", "US"]}, {"type": "ipa", "text": "/ðen/", "tags": ["General Australian"]}], "forms": [{"word": "den", "tags": ["alternative"]}], "senses": [{"definition": "Obsolete spelling of than.", "tags": ["alt of", "obsolete"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "[…]his hand, more ſad [i.e., heavy, hard] then lomp of lead,[…]", "reference": "1590, Edmund Spenser, “Book II, Canto VIII”, in The Faerie Queene. […], London: […] [John Wolfe] for William Ponsonbie, →OCLC, stanza 30, page 299:"}, {"text": "And as a Pible caſt into a Spring, / Wee ſee a ſort of trembling cirkles riſe, / One forming other in theyr iſſuing / Till ouer all the Fount they circulize, / So this perpetuall-motion-making kiſſe, / Is propagate through all my faculties, / And makes my breaſt an endleſſe Fount of bliſſe, / Of which, if Gods could drink, theyr matchleſſe fare / Would make them much more bleſſed then they are.", "reference": "1595, Ouids Banquet of Sence. A Coronet for his Miſtreſſe Philoſophie, and his amorous Zodiacke. VVith a tranſlation of a Latine coppie, written by a Fryer, Anno Dom. 1400, London: I. R. for Richard Smith:"}, {"text": "Clow[ne]. O they haue lyud long on the almſbaſket of wordes. I maruaile thy M.hath not eaten thee for a worde, for thou art not ſo long by the head as honorificabilitudinitatibus: Thou art eaſier ſwallowed then a flapdragon.", "reference": "c. 1595–1596 (date written), W. Shakespere [i.e., William Shakespeare], A Pleasant Conceited Comedie Called, Loues Labors Lost. […] (First Quarto), London: […] W[illiam] W[hite] for Cut[h]bert Burby, published 1598, →OCLC, [Act V, scene i]:"}, {"text": "To ſet the minde on the racke of long meditation (you ſay) is a torment: to follow the ſwift foote of your hound alday long, hath no wearineſſe: what would you ſay of him that finds better game in his ſtudie, then you in the fielde, and would account your diſport his puniſhment? ſuch there are, though you doubt and wonder.", "reference": "1611, Joseph Hall, “Epistle VIII. To E.B. Dedicated to Sir George Goring.”, in Epistles […], volume III, London: […] [William Stansby and William Jaggard] for Samuell Macham, […], →OCLC, 5th decade, pages 95–96:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "Misspelling of than.", "tags": ["alt of", "misspelling"], "examples": [], "quotes": [], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": []}], "source": {"url": "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/then", "license": {"name": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/"}}}}